1
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:04,254
<i>Caloy, I don't understand.</i>

2
00:00:04,337 --> 00:00:07,632
<i>I want Billy's life</i>
<i>because it should've been mine.</i>

3
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:10,218
<i>But Billy just had to steal it!</i>

4
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:14,222
[JORDAN]
<i>Bea's mom's name is Mariela Mercado.</i>

5
00:00:14,305 --> 00:00:18,727
<i>She was confined for three years</i>
<i>in a mental institution.</i>

6
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:20,603
[BILLY] <i>That's serious, Jordan.</i>

7
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:22,522
[JORDAN]
<i>But there's nothing we can do right now</i>

8
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,983
<i>except be careful.</i>

9
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:26,609
<i>Uh, sir…</i>

10
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:30,780
<i>About the advance pay I was asking for…</i>

11
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:32,741
<i>Could I please receive it today?</i>

12
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:42,625
<i>This is the last time I'll do this, okay?</i>
<i>I'm making a loss because of you!</i>

13
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:45,128
<i>I'm sorry, sir.</i>

14
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:48,840
<i>It's just that my mother</i>
<i>still hasn't recovered.</i>

15
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:51,009
<i>She keeps going back to the hospital.</i>

16
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:52,719
<i>And where is your father?</i>

17
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:57,724
- <i>You bought a lot, huh?</i>
- <i>Daddy! </i>[YOUNG BILLY GIGGLES]

18
00:00:57,807 --> 00:00:59,517
- [OLIVE]<i> My goodness.</i>
<i>- Pa?</i>

19
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:02,103
- [OLIVE] <i>She's such a daddy's girl!</i>
- [ENRICO] <i>Are you happy now?</i>

20
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:03,813
<i>- Yes. Thank you, Daddy.</i>
<i>- Pa?</i>

21
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:07,317
- [WOMAN] <i>Oh! Watch where you're going.</i>
- [ENRICO] <i>Okay, let's go.</i>

22
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,735
[YOUNG BILLY, ENRICO LAUGHING]

23
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:10,320
- [OLIVE] <i>We're so happy.</i>
<i>- Pa!</i>

24
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:12,614
<i>Pa. Pa! </i>[PANTING]

25
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:13,740
<i>Pa!</i>

26
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:16,201
<i>Pa!</i>

27
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:25,877
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

28
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:32,759
<i>…we are preparing something</i>
<i>bigger and better for LoveList.</i>

29
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:37,555
<i>And I'm sure that here, love is better,</i>

30
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,599
<i>whether it's the first</i>
<i>or second time around,</i>

31
00:01:39,682 --> 00:01:42,477
<i>as long as you are with the right one…</i>

32
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,021
[CROWD] <i>At the right time.</i>

33
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:48,650
[CROWD CHEERING]

34
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:55,073
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

35
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:56,741
<i>Sir Jordan.</i>

36
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:59,160
<i>You need to sign a few papers</i>
<i>for the transfer.</i>

37
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,454
<i>- Okay. Grandpa?</i>
<i>- This way, please.</i>

38
00:02:02,413 --> 00:02:03,540
<i>I'll be back, okay?</i>

39
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:15,468
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

40
00:02:20,014 --> 00:02:21,057
<i>Dude.</i>

41
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:23,476
<i>Dude?</i>

42
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,728
<i>- Sir Jordan, your grandpa…</i>
<i>- What's wrong?</i>

43
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:28,481
<i>He escaped.</i>
<i>But security is already looking for him.</i>

44
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:29,566
<i>What?!</i>

45
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,693
<i>Jordan?</i>

46
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:33,111
<i>Are you okay?</i>

47
00:02:33,736 --> 00:02:35,572
<i>Sorry. Grandpa Jude is missing.</i>

48
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:36,698
<i>What?!</i>

49
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:39,075
<i>All right, I'm on my way.</i>

50
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:41,578
- Hurry up.
- Okay, sir.

51
00:02:41,661 --> 00:02:43,663
Why were you being so careless?!

52
00:02:43,746 --> 00:02:45,415
- I'm so sorry.
- This shouldn't be happening.

53
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:47,167
We are responsible for this.

54
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,334
- I told you--
- Well?

55
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:49,752
You still haven't found my grandpa?!

56
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:51,504
Sir, we're very, very sorry.

57
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:54,299
But we're still looking for him.
We are looking for him, sir.

58
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:56,676
- I'm sorry.
- Sir, I'll help out too.

59
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:58,094
No!

60
00:02:58,177 --> 00:02:59,554
Just stay away!

61
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:00,638
[NURSE] No one's picking up.

62
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:01,681
Go!

63
00:03:01,764 --> 00:03:05,894
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:07,061
This shouldn't be happening!

65
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:11,149
Excuse me. Excuse me.

66
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,026
Have you seen this man?

67
00:03:13,109 --> 00:03:14,193
- No.
- No.

68
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:15,778
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

69
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:18,072
All right.

70
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:20,909
Excuse me.

71
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:22,535
Can you help me? Ah…

72
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:23,953
Have you seen him?

73
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:26,414
- No. I haven't.
- No?

74
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:28,082
- Are you sure?
- Yes, I'm sure.

75
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,375
All right, thank you.

76
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:34,130
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:35,256
Jordan!

78
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,717
Dude, I can't find him!

79
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:40,136
Please, I can't lose him too.

80
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,930
Jordan, breathe. Breathe.

81
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:43,723
[JORDAN INHALES, EXHALES SHARPLY]

82
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:45,475
We'll find him, okay?

83
00:03:45,558 --> 00:03:47,727
Let's split up so we can find him faster.

84
00:03:47,810 --> 00:03:49,062
I'll go this way, you go that way.

85
00:03:49,145 --> 00:03:51,356
Breathe. We'll find him.

86
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:52,398
Let's go.

87
00:03:52,482 --> 00:03:56,486
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

88
00:03:56,569 --> 00:04:03,284
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

89
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:43,283
Miss, have you seen him?

90
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:44,951
Oh. Isn't that him?

91
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:46,494
- [BILLY] Yes. Thank you!
- [WOMAN 1] Sure.

92
00:04:46,577 --> 00:04:48,579
Grandpa! Grandpa Jude!

93
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:49,998
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:04:50,081 --> 00:04:51,040
Oh.

95
00:04:51,791 --> 00:04:52,709
Billy.

96
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:54,085
Hi, Grandpa!

97
00:04:54,168 --> 00:04:55,878
Are you okay?

98
00:04:55,962 --> 00:04:57,880
How are you feeling?

99
00:04:57,964 --> 00:05:00,008
We've been looking for you.

100
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:02,302
Jordan is worried about you.

101
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,763
I'll just call him, okay?

102
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:12,437
I saw my son-in-law again.

103
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:14,772
- Hmm.
- I saw Dino.

104
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:19,402
Jordan's father.

105
00:05:22,071 --> 00:05:24,532
He's not a good husband.

106
00:05:24,615 --> 00:05:26,284
And he's not a good father either.

107
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:30,538
That's why I took Jordan away from him.

108
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:34,751
But he's tried to reach out several times.

109
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:38,087
That's probably why I saw him earlier.

110
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:40,590
It got me thinking.

111
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:44,802
What if he came back
because he has changed?

112
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:50,391
Who am I to deny my grandson's right
to see his father?

113
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:54,103
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:56,272
My grandson grew up

115
00:05:57,982 --> 00:06:01,861
with hatred for his father.

116
00:06:05,281 --> 00:06:07,116
It's hard to live

117
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:10,369
with resentment in your heart.

118
00:06:13,831 --> 00:06:15,917
Is what I did wrong, Billy?

119
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:23,549
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

120
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:35,561
[BILLY] <i>Just leave.</i>

121
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:37,396
<i>Stay away from my family.</i>

122
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,232
<i>Billy, what's going on?</i>

123
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:41,901
<i>How could you be so selfish?</i>

124
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:43,569
<i>Seriously?</i>

125
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:47,949
<i>You even made a fool of the person</i>
<i>who raised us and cared for us</i>

126
00:06:48,032 --> 00:06:49,700
<i>when that should have been you?!</i>

127
00:06:50,326 --> 00:06:52,245
<i>I didn't mean to fool anyone.</i>

128
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:57,542
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:06:57,625 --> 00:06:58,584
Grandpa!

130
00:06:59,752 --> 00:07:01,796
- Dude, is he okay?
- Yes.

131
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:02,839
Grandpa.

132
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:04,674
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

133
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:07,510
I've been looking for you everywhere.

134
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:13,516
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:22,650
Can I join?

136
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:24,777
[BILLY GIGGLES]

137
00:07:24,861 --> 00:07:26,904
[JUDE] Oh. Where did I go?

138
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:33,619
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

139
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:37,540
- Come on, let's go.
- Let's go, Grandpa.

140
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:44,797
As for me,

141
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,717
my parents disowned me when I was a kid.

142
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:50,344
Life was hard because I was alone.

143
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:51,679
I don't have anyone,

144
00:07:51,762 --> 00:07:55,224
so my life became worthless.

145
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:58,144
But everything changed
when I met this girl.

146
00:07:58,936 --> 00:07:59,979
I learned to love.

147
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:02,356
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

148
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:03,900
See?

149
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:06,027
She's pretty, isn't she? [SNIFFLES]

150
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:09,780
[CHUCKLES]
But sadly, I'm here in jail.

151
00:08:10,364 --> 00:08:12,158
I can't be with her.

152
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:16,537
As the pastor said, "I have a voice."

153
00:08:16,621 --> 00:08:17,663
[PASTOR] Amen.

154
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:21,083
And Dino said

155
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:23,252
that as long as we're alive,
there's still hope.

156
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:24,795
[PASTOR] Amen.

157
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:26,464
So I'll marry her

158
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:29,217
once I find a way to escape from here.

159
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:35,973
- [UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [LAUGHTER]

160
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:45,733
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:08:45,816 --> 00:08:48,611
AMIHAN HOME

162
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:58,579
I think this place is really better.

163
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:01,165
Grandpa Jude will be safer here.

164
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:03,501
I hope so.

165
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,216
I'm glad you were there.

166
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:12,343
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

167
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:13,844
If it weren't for you,

168
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:16,597
I could've lost both my mother

169
00:09:17,181 --> 00:09:18,933
and my grandpa.

170
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:23,771
Thank you so much.

171
00:09:23,854 --> 00:09:27,733
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

172
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:32,238
Good thing I'm here, right?

173
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:36,534
What would you do without me?

174
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,202
[TEASINGLY] Hmm?

175
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:40,955
- Tell me.
- Fine.

176
00:09:41,038 --> 00:09:42,957
Yeah. [CHUCKLES]

177
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:50,006
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:55,595
[JUDE] <i>Who am I to deny</i>
<i>my grandson's right</i>

179
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:56,721
<i>to see his father?</i>

180
00:09:56,804 --> 00:09:58,472
<i>It's hard to live</i>

181
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:01,225
<i>with resentment in your heart.</i>

182
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:03,728
<i>Is what I did wrong, Billy?</i>

183
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,981
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

184
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,651
Oliver.

185
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:12,695
You're not going to school.

186
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:14,697
Why?

187
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:18,409
You know the reason, right?

188
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:20,953
But I have to go to school.

189
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:22,913
Your sister and I need to make sure

190
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:24,790
that your father
is no longer working there.

191
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:25,916
I'm going.

192
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,919
Oliver, you're not going to school today.

193
00:10:30,671 --> 00:10:32,548
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

194
00:10:36,135 --> 00:10:43,100
[MISCHIEVOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

195
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:54,695
[DOOR OPENS]

196
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:59,784
[MISCHIEVOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

197
00:10:59,867 --> 00:11:02,161
We've addressed your concern, Ms. Cariño.

198
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:05,581
<i>We terminated Mr. Dominguez's employment</i>
<i>immediately.</i>

199
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:08,334
<i>He didn't only submit forged documents,</i>

200
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:11,003
but he also hid his criminal history.

201
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:13,255
Okay. Thank you, Ms. Ronquillo.

202
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:16,300
We prioritize the safety
and protection of our students,

203
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:19,220
<i>so we've alerted security across</i>
<i>the entire school campus.</i>

204
00:11:19,303 --> 00:11:22,014
<i>And I want to assure you,</i>

205
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:23,849
he's never setting foot in here again.

206
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:29,939
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

207
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:31,065
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

208
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:33,651
- Billy.
- Auntie.

209
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:34,944
Billy…

210
00:11:35,861 --> 00:11:40,241
Your brother's throwing a tantrum,
insisting on going to school.

211
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:42,993
We both know why he wants to, right?

212
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:47,998
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

213
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:54,880
[MUSIC BECOMES MISCHIEVOUS]

214
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:56,340
Oliver?

215
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:58,259
Auntie Pres!

216
00:11:58,342 --> 00:12:00,219
Auntie, where's Oliver?

217
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:01,595
My God.

218
00:12:03,305 --> 00:12:05,099
[LINE RINGING, BUSY TONE]

219
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:07,184
He's not picking up.

220
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:09,103
[BUSY TONE]

221
00:12:09,186 --> 00:12:15,526
[MISCHIEVOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

222
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:33,836
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:42,386
Didn't I tell you not to go to work today?

224
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,305
I'm the one who'll get in trouble.

225
00:12:44,388 --> 00:12:46,474
I'll figure something out.

226
00:12:47,349 --> 00:12:48,851
I'll talk to the principal.

227
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:50,728
She won't listen to you.

228
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:53,022
I still have to try.

229
00:12:53,105 --> 00:12:57,693
The only place Oliver and I can meet
is on campus.

230
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:01,864
Pa?

231
00:13:02,531 --> 00:13:08,662
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING, THEN FADES]

232
00:13:11,499 --> 00:13:13,250
Why did you leave us?

233
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:16,086
Why did you do that to Billy?

234
00:13:18,255 --> 00:13:19,507
I'm sorry, son.

235
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:24,512
When Mama passed away,
we ended up out on the streets.

236
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:26,263
We lived on the streets.

237
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:30,059
Where were you
when we really needed you most?

238
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:33,270
Why didn't you ever come for us?

239
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:36,190
I made mistakes, son.

240
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:39,318
I admit it.

241
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:42,363
I wasn't a good man back then.

242
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:46,116
I hurt so many people.

243
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,118
I wasn't a good father.

244
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:52,790
I turned my back on my duty
as your father.

245
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:56,252
That's why I'm asking
for your forgiveness.

246
00:13:57,836 --> 00:14:00,339
You lied to Auntie as well?

247
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:05,719
I had no other way to get close to you.

248
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,597
I just wanted us to be together.

249
00:14:10,724 --> 00:14:12,685
So I had to pretend.

250
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:16,397
I didn't tell you I was your dad
because I was afraid

251
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:20,568
you'd react just like Billy
if I told you the truth.

252
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:22,903
You'd just push me away.

253
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:25,781
I love you, son.

254
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:29,076
You and Billy, both of you.

255
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:32,454
I'd do anything to earn your forgiveness.

256
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:36,417
[SOBS SOFTLY]

257
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:43,424
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:49,096
[ENRICO SNIFFLES]

259
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:57,146
[ENRICO SNIFFLES]

260
00:14:59,356 --> 00:15:01,066
[CAR DOORS CLOSE]

261
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:06,322
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

262
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:20,127
[SNIFFLES, COUGHS]

263
00:15:23,213 --> 00:15:24,798
[BREATHES SOFTLY]

264
00:15:24,882 --> 00:15:29,470
You know why I want to study at
the University of Kingsley?

265
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:34,850
Because I want to come visit you there.

266
00:15:36,018 --> 00:15:36,936
What?

267
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:41,649
Billy told me
that's where you were buried.

268
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:45,319
[SNIFFLES]

269
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:47,529
I don't blame your sister.

270
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:51,033
So don't hold that against her.

271
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:55,371
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

272
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:56,622
Why?

273
00:15:56,705 --> 00:15:59,249
Aren't you going to push through
your scholarship?

274
00:15:59,833 --> 00:16:01,585
O-Of course.

275
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:07,132
I will, so Auntie and Billy
can be proud of me.

276
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:09,718
And you too, Pa.

277
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:16,725
Listen, no matter where you go to school,

278
00:16:17,309 --> 00:16:19,061
I'll always be proud of you.

279
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:22,356
I was proud of Billy.
And I'm proud of Precious.

280
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:26,110
They raised you right.

281
00:16:27,277 --> 00:16:29,613
The way I should have.

282
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,617
So…

283
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:37,830
So I don't blame your sister

284
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:41,166
for thinking you didn't need me anymore.

285
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:46,505
Because she already made
you whole all on her own.

286
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:52,428
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

287
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:55,222
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

288
00:16:59,476 --> 00:17:00,936
Truth is…

289
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:07,151
I… I'm the one
who feels incomplete because…

290
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:11,363
I'm the one who won't feel whole
until you forgive me.

291
00:17:13,782 --> 00:17:16,285
But I won't force you to.

292
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:20,122
Pa…

293
00:17:21,623 --> 00:17:23,500
I already forgave you.

294
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:25,502
And besides,

295
00:17:26,211 --> 00:17:28,547
I told you, remember?

296
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:30,549
I'll help you.

297
00:17:31,675 --> 00:17:33,093
Billy has a good heart,

298
00:17:34,678 --> 00:17:37,681
even if she can be a tiger sometimes.

299
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:40,100
[CHUCKLING]

300
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:45,939
You know, that courage you have?

301
00:17:46,982 --> 00:17:48,108
[OLIVER CHUCKLES]

302
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:51,028
- You got that from Billy.
- Yes.

303
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:53,906
She was the first one
to teach me self-defense.

304
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:56,241
Is that why you punched Biboy?

305
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:57,785
[OLIVER] It wasn't just that, Pa.

306
00:17:57,868 --> 00:18:00,287
She also talked back to Biboy's dad.

307
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:02,331
She didn't back down at all.

308
00:18:02,414 --> 00:18:06,001
You know, she was already a fighter
when she was still just a kid.

309
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:06,919
[OLIVER] A fighter?

310
00:18:07,002 --> 00:18:10,422
Yes. Your mom and I were called
to school because of her.

311
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:12,800
We were called because she got
into a fight. She got bullied.

312
00:18:12,883 --> 00:18:15,469
Bullied by two classmates. Boys.

313
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:17,930
- Boys? And there were two?
- Two boys.

314
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:23,143
And we were surprised
because when we got there,

315
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:26,688
the boys had more bruises than Billy did!

316
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:28,023
- She punched them?
- She sure did!

317
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:30,317
Both ended up with black eyes.

318
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:33,070
One for each eye? [CHUCKLES]

319
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:36,323
Ready to go, Auntie?

320
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:37,908
[ENRICO] Think you can do that?

321
00:18:37,991 --> 00:18:40,410
- [OLIVER] Sure I can.
- [ENRICO] Bullseye both times!

322
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:44,456
[OLIVER] Did those two boys cry?
That must've hurt, huh?

323
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:47,960
- [OLIVER LAUGHS]
- Look at you. You really take after Billy.

324
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:50,838
You're sure about this, Billy?

325
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:53,465
You don't want Oliver to go home for now?

326
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:57,386
What else can I do, Auntie?

327
00:18:58,303 --> 00:19:01,306
He's so stubborn. Such an obstinate kid!

328
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:05,686
Wonder where he got that from?

329
00:19:06,728 --> 00:19:11,191
Well, at least he knows
how to fight for what he wants.

330
00:19:11,275 --> 00:19:14,862
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

331
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:17,447
He's growing up, Auntie Pres.

332
00:19:18,115 --> 00:19:19,867
He makes his own choices now.

333
00:19:23,787 --> 00:19:25,122
You okay with this?

334
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,876
For now.

335
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:33,505
Look how happy he was with his dad.

336
00:19:36,091 --> 00:19:38,343
I can't take that away from him, Auntie.

337
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:43,849
[UPLIFTING MUSIC CONTINUES]

338
00:19:52,065 --> 00:19:53,358
[JORDAN] <i>Compartmentalizing.</i>

339
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:56,236
<i>So easy to just turn off a problem,</i>
<i>focus on another…</i>

340
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:58,739
[BILLY] <i>It was wrong for me</i>
<i>to make decisions for him.</i>

341
00:19:58,822 --> 00:20:00,991
<i>Because all he wants is</i>
<i>to know his dad.</i>

342
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:05,370
<i>Are you convinced that</i>
<i>your dad is truly remorseful?</i>

343
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:06,747
<i>- Ma.</i>
<i>- Where's your laundry?</i>

344
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:07,956
<i>I'll do the laundry.</i>

345
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:12,544
<i>Why'd you choose to join our group?</i>

346
00:20:12,628 --> 00:20:14,671
<i>From what I can see,</i>
<i>you're the nicest people here.</i>

347
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:17,466
<i>They told me to behave</i>
<i>so my sentence might be reduced.</i>

348
00:20:17,549 --> 00:20:18,759
<i>What do you know?</i>

349
00:20:18,842 --> 00:20:20,928
<i>Thanks, Lucy, for all your help.</i>

350
00:20:21,011 --> 00:20:23,513
<i>If your oldest daughter</i>
<i>talks to the principal,</i>

351
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:24,932
<i>she might change her mind.</i>

352
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:26,308
<i>She might reconsider.</i>

353
00:20:26,391 --> 00:20:28,602
<i>LoveList was built in the Philippines,</i>

354
00:20:28,685 --> 00:20:32,856
<i>but the chase for real connection</i>
<i>is not uniquely Filipino.</i>

355
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:36,735
<i>Our mindset is global</i>
<i>from day one, Mr. Fabrizio.</i>

356
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:40,239
<i>The phone isn't the problem!</i>
<i>You know what the problem is?!</i>

357
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:42,282
<i>That annoying app!</i>

358
00:20:42,366 --> 00:20:44,826
<i>LoveList isn't just trying</i>
<i>to match people.</i>

359
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:47,371
<i>We're trying to</i>
<i>get to know them more.</i>

360
00:20:47,454 --> 00:20:51,333
<i>After reviewing your proposal</i>
<i>and hearing you talk now…</i>
